    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (79.74) and **Kyle Schwarber** (75.72) anchoring our offensive attack. Both benefit immensely from a favorable encounter with Tomoyuki Sugano; the combination of a generous opposing xERA and high-leverage spots at the top of the lineup drives their elite daily efficiency scores. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a priority start (68.60) despite the L/L matchup against Andrew Abbott, as his elite 0.428 xwOBA provides the ceiling necessary to carry our power categories regardless of platoon splits. Conversely, we are leaning into **Dillon Dingler** (61.00) and **Junior Caminero** (60.60) as high-upside plays; while the latter faces a tough matchup against Payton Tolle, **Junior Caminero**\u2019s premium lineup slotting keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (35.65), who failed to crack the active lineup due to the formidable presence of Logan Gilbert on the mound. While **Chase Meidroth** offers utility, the significant negative adjustment for SP skill (-19%) against Gilbert made him an easy exclusion in favor of higher-floor assets. We are closely monitoring the status of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (49.80); while his speed is a critical asset for our stolen base targets, his matchup against the elite Jacob deGrom forces him into a marginal start position. With **Christian Yelich**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Zac Veen** currently unavailable due to injury or minor league assignment, our depth is being tested, making it imperative that **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, and **Hyeseong Kim** capitalize on their respective platoons to avoid burning game caps. We are proceeding with caution regarding these \"Lineup Pending\" designations, as any shift down the order for **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, or **Luke Raley** could necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of our efficiency thresholds.",
